  "answer": "In Q1 2026, citation reliability was the single most prominent customer complaint [NL-010#NL-010-S01], with a sharp increase in citation-error tickets and a breakdown showing incorrect file links (42%), missing page numbers (28%), empty citations (18%), and broken links (12%) [NL-010#NL-010-S05]. This caused enterprise trust issues, including paused pilots [NL-010#NL-010-S05].\n\nIn Q2 2026, after the April 2026 product fixes, citation-related complaints decreased significantly and citation accuracy stabilized [NL-011#NL-011-S01][NL-011#NL-011-S03]. Citation accuracy tickets fell from 88 in March (and 42 in April) to 24 in June [NL-011#NL-011-S05]. Overall NPS rose from 41 to 44, driven by the April fix addressing critical citation reliability issues [NL-011#NL-011-S01]. However, citation issues did not fully disappear: remaining tickets were nearly all linked to scanned, image-only PDFs where citation anchors fail, and there was minor lag in citation indexing during peak hours after document updates [NL-011#NL-011-S05][NL-016#NL-016-S04].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
